fact WorkItem(id: "WI-098", description: some(value: "Proposal 025.1 Phase 3 — Pass-through tactics + raw escape hatch. Validates the IR end-to-end before tackling meta-tactics. Deliverables: anthill-smt-gen emit_tactic(Tactic) -> String serialiser maps IR to Z3 input syntax — Smt(args) to (check-sat-using (using-params smt :timeout :random_seed)); Simplify/qe/propagate-values to (using-params <name> ...); Then to (then a b); OrElse to (or-else a b); Repeat{tactic, times} to (repeat <t> <n>); Par to (par-or a b); Raw(s) verbatim splice. Update lf1 existing proofs to dispatch through the new emitter (no behavioural change; validates the IR). Acceptance: discharge.sh reports 5/5 unsat unchanged; new tests cover each pass-through tactic shape. Risks: Z3 tactic naming drift across versions (mitigation: z3 --version captured in cache key, version bump → entries miss → re-run). See §Implementation plan Phase 3."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-097"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-04-27T19:32:01Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-098", author: "claude", content: "Phase 3 pass-through tactic emit shipped. Module: anthill-smt-gen/src/tactic_emit.rs. Two API entry points: emit_tactic_expr (parse-side, walks Tactic IR from WI-097) and emit_tactic_from_term (CLI-side, walks runtime KB Term::Fn). Both produce the body of (check-sat-using ...) — Bare/App/Raw lower to Z3 syntax: smt → 'smt' or '(using-params smt :random_seed 42)'; then/or_else/par → '(then a b)'/'(or-else a b)'/'(par-or a b)' (anthill→Z3 keyword translation); repeat(t, times: 5) → '(repeat t 5)'; raw('...') splices verbatim. Trivial-default elision: bare smt with only logic/timeout returns None → caller emits plain (check-sat) (preserves the lf1 byte-stream + cache hits). Combinator children DON'T elide — emit_term_force/emit_tactic_force always produce a string so 'then(simplify, smt)' becomes '(then simplify smt)'. ProofConfig.tactic_expr threads the rendered string through render_satisfiability_with + render_upper_bound_with: when Some(expr), close with (check-sat-using <expr>); when None, plain (check-sat). CLI dispatch_z3 reads the runtime ProofRecord's args, looks for 'tactic:' named arg, walks the value term via emit_tactic_from_term. Pre-existing bug fixed: read_named_arg's syms.named_arg cache returned None for bare-interned 'named_arg', causing tool_args to silently empty; now also matches by short-name suffix. ArgValue gained Term(TermId) variant so non-primitive named-arg values flow through. Tests: 9 unit (parse-side) + 6 E2E (real CLI + dry-run, including legacy_lf1_proofs_unchanged anchor). Workspace 809 tests, 0 regressions.", at: "2026-04-27T19:32:01Z")
